<back><div type="verses">
<lg label="2."><l>Once darkness, we did walk in hate,</l><l>Far from Your holy flame.</l><l>Light quelled sin’s gloom; our needs You sate,</l><l>Born of Your radiant name,</l><l>Not merely children of the day,</l><l>But light itself—we rise!</l><l>Awake, o sleeper, from the dead:</l><l>Light shines! Light makes us Christ!</l></lg>
<lg label="3."><l>True Life in us, unconquerable,</l><l>Each blow Christ can endure;</l><l>No storm, no hell, no tempter’s pull</l><l>Can shake Life’s power pure.</l><l>Our mortal life, Light’s tests expose,</l><l>Its frailty laid so bare!</l><l>Our strength dissolves, but Christ bestows</l><l>A life beyond death’s snare.</l></lg>
<lg label="4."><l>As light reveals, Your life supplies,</l><l>A pathway sure and bright.</l><l>From depths of love, we realize</l><l>Our growth is borne by light.</l><l>In light, no veil now hides Your face—</l><l>Our sight, restored and clear!</l><l>Through You, we walk, transformed in grace,</l><l>Your glory drawing near!</l></lg>
</div>
</back>
</music></mei>
